contentText:
50 Cent threw on the boxing gloves and performed his own stunts in the upcoming Street Fighter movie. Paramount Pictures released a trailer on Tuesday (Sept. 1) for the live-action remake based on the famed video game series.

Street Fighter is slated to hit U.S. theaters on Oct. 16. The action-packed teaser is based around Chun-Li, who is played by Callina Liang, attempting to convince Ryu (Andrew Koji) that Ken Masters (Noah Centineo) finds himself in a precarious situation and needs help ASAP traversing the World Warrior Tournament.

