Starring as Balrog, 50 pops up for a pair of scenes in the trailer, one of which finds him dishing out a beatdown to Ken Masters in the boxing ring.

Sporting the hilarious M-shaped hairline, another clip shows 50 suited up and heading to the club, where WWE superstar Cody Rhodes makes an appearance. Comedian Eric Andre even shines as the in-ring announcer for the fights.

Per The Hollywood Reporter , 50 underwent intense training to hold up in the ring and make sure there was no need for a stunt double. As far as rounding out the rest of the cast, WWE&#8217;s Roman Reigns (Joe Anoa&#8217;i), Jason Momoa and country singer Orville Peck&nbsp;also star in Street Fighter.

The G-Unit boss will also be contributing to the Street Fighter soundtrack. During a July appearance on Today With Jenna and Sheinelle , 50 revealed a tantalizing posthumous collaboration with 2Pac and Eminem.

“I got some music that I’m working on. I did something currently me, Eminem and 2Pac,” he teased. &#8220;I got some music that I’m working on. I did something currently me, Eminem and 2Pac.&#8221;

50 and Em have remained close over the years, while colliding for tracks like “Don’t Push Me,” “Patiently Waiting,” “Gatman & Robin” and “You Don’t Know.”

